Package: xrdbi
Title: 'DBI' Backend for 'xarray' via a Live 'reticulate' Session
Version: 0.0.1.9019
Authors@R: c(
    person("Michael", "Sumner", email = "mdsumner@gmail.com",
           role = c("aut", "cre")),
    person("The GDAL/OGR contributors", role = "cph",
           comment = "test fixtures in inst/extdata/autotest, see inst/COPYRIGHTS")
    )
Description: Treats a live Python session holding an 'xarray'
    <https://xarray.dev> object as a database connection. Tables are
    variables, fields are dimensions and coordinates, and queries are
    Python expressions (or compiled from a small structured spec or from
    'dplyr' verbs) evaluated lazily against the dataset. Fetching renders
    the tidy long form, one row per cell, built in R from the values;
    results can also render as an in-memory raster.
License: MIT + file LICENSE
Encoding: UTF-8
Roxygen: list(markdown = TRUE)
Depends:
    R (>= 4.1.0)
Imports:
    DBI (>= 1.2.0),
    dplyr,
    methods,
    reticulate (>= 1.41.0),
    rlang, 
    utils
Suggests:
    sf,
    testthat (>= 3.0.0),
    wk
Config/testthat/edition: 3
SystemRequirements: Python (>= 3.11) with the 'xarray' and 'netCDF4'
    modules, declared on load with reticulate::py_require() and
    provisioned automatically when no Python is configured. Other IO
    engines are declared as needed (e.g. 'zarr', 'h5netcdf'); the
    'gdalxarray' engine also needs the GDAL Python bindings, which pip
    cannot install.
URL: https://github.com/mdsumner/xrdbi
BugReports: https://github.com/mdsumner/xrdbi/issues
Config/roxygen2/version: 8.0.0
